Source directory: /opt/ddk/src/android16-6.12
Original source hashes: upstream/SOURCES.json (before local adaptations)

The upstream files retain their original license notices. The local changes are:
- Store netns_nftables in registered net_generic storage. CONFIG_NF_TABLES
  remains disabled so the native struct net layout is not changed.
- Restore the private nf_tables header helpers omitted by that configuration.
- Combine extension registration into one module with reverse-order rollback
  and teardown. Cleanup functions are retained for initialization failures.
- Supply the omitted INET NAT registration wrapper using native IPv4/IPv6
  NAT hooks and private hook arrays (nat-inet.c).

Build: scripts/build-ddk.sh TARGET=netfilter OUT=/module/out/netfilter -j4
This produces droidspaces_netfilter.ko. Native imports require ksud insmod;
ordinary insmod cannot resolve the private, unexported kernel symbols.
The release/device guard is limited to the verified PLZ110 kernel and QEMU GKI.
ABI checks against the target BTF remain mandatory before device installation.

Supported families: IPv4, IPv6, INET. Includes xt_addrtype, nftables core,
sets, conntrack, NAT/masquerade/redirect, FIB, reject, logging, limit and xtables
compatibility. Does not implement bridge/netdev nftables or br_netfilter.
No new firewall rules are installed by module initialization. Rule programming
and module references remain managed by the native netfilter infrastructure.

Regression entry point: tests/vm/run-netfilter.sh
The Debian ARM64 fixture must contain Docker, iproute2, iptables-legacy,
iptables-nft, nftables, curl, Python 3, and the offline busybox:1.37.0 image
archive at /opt/ds-docker-test/images.tar. QEMU uses a disposable disk snapshot.
